## Advanced Operations

### Linear Algebra

```python
import numpy as np
from numpy.linalg import norm, matrix_rank, solve

# Matrix operations
A = np.array([[1, 2], [3, 4]])
B = np.array([[5, 6], [7, 8]])

# Matrix multiplication
C = np.dot(A, B)      # or A @ B
# [[19 22]
#  [43 50]]

# Element-wise multiplication
element_wise = A * B
# [[5 12]
#  [21 32]]

# Transpose
A_T = A.T

# Determinant
det = np.linalg.det(A)  # -2.0

# Inverse
A_inv = np.linalg.inv(A)

# Eigenvalues & Eigenvectors
eigenvalues, eigenvectors = np.linalg.eig(A)

# Matrix rank
rank = matrix_rank(A)  # 2

# Trace (sum of diagonal)
trace = np.trace(A)    # 5

# Norm (vector length)
v = np.array([3, 4])
vec_norm = norm(v)     # 5.0

# Solve linear system: Ax = b
b = np.array([1, 2])
x = solve(A, b)

# Decompositions
U, s, Vt = np.linalg.svd(A)  # Singular Value Decomposition
Q, R = np.linalg.qr(A)        # QR Decomposition
L = np.linalg.cholesky(A)     # Cholesky Decomposition
```

