## Performance & Optimization

### Memory Views & Copies

```python
arr = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])

# View (shares data, no copy)
view = arr[:]
view[0] = 999  # Changes original array

# Copy (independent data)
copy = arr.copy()
copy[0] = 999  # Doesn't change original

# Check if array is C-contiguous
print(arr.flags['C_CONTIGUOUS'])  # True (faster operations)

# Make C-contiguous
c_cont = np.ascontiguousarray(arr)
```

