arr = arr[:, np.newaxis]  # (3, 1)

# Right: Know what shape you need
arr = arr[:, np.newaxis]  # (3, 1) - column
arr = arr[np.newaxis, :]  # (1, 3) - row
```

**Pitfall 2: Not Using keepdims**
```python
# Without keepdims (loses dimension)
means = data.mean(axis=1)  # Shape (n,) instead of (n, 1)

# With keepdims (preserves dimension)
means = data.mean(axis=1, keepdims=True)  # Shape (n, 1)
# Now broadcasting works correctly!
```

**Pitfall 3: Copy vs View Confusion**
```python
# Surprising behavior
arr = np.arange(10)
sliced = arr[2:5]
sliced[0] = 999
print(arr[2])  # 999! (view, not copy)

# Solution: Use .copy() when needed
sliced = arr[2:5].copy()
```

